# Comparisons do not chain; the help rewrites the chain with and.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where a < b < c
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..20
  PIPELINE@0..19
    NAME_REF@0..1
      IDENT@0..1 "t"
    WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
    PIPE@2..3 "|"
    WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
    WHERE_OP@4..19
      IDENT@4..9 "where"
      WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
      BIN_EXPR@10..19
        BIN_EXPR@10..15
          NAME_REF@10..11
            IDENT@10..11 "a"
          WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
          LT@12..13 "<"
          WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
          NAME_REF@14..15
            IDENT@14..15 "b"
        WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
        LT@16..17 "<"
        WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
        NAME_REF@18..19
          IDENT@18..19 "c"
  WHITESPACE@19..20 "\n"

error[DS0101]: comparison operators cannot be chained
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | t | where a < b < c
  |           ----- ^ a second comparison
  |           |
  |           the result of this comparison is not a value to compare again
  |
  = help: compare each pair separately: `a < b and b < c`
